; ---- measurement hook: DZ_PRIM_PROF --------------------------------------
; Not a feature. The Scaly half of the per-primitive time profile; the whole
; mechanism and the reason it is a sampler rather than a clock are documented
; in tests/dazzle/primprof/primprof.c.
;
; What it answers: the leaf profile of 2026-08-05 puts the port's remaining
; deficit in the ENGINE (93 % of the excess instructions) and, inside it,
; names "die Primitiven selbst" — 1.72 G against the reference's 0.23 G. That
; is a SUM over 226 primitives and gives no target. This splits it.
;
; The hot path is three instructions: `enter` charges a call and publishes the
; id, `exit` restores the previous one. A 1 ms ITIMER_PROF signal samples the
; published id, so the result is CPU time per primitive, immune to the fact
; that `opt` inlines the primitive bodies into Primitive.dispatch (which is
; what makes an external profiler useless here — see the misdiagnosis noted in
; PERFORMANCE.md under "Ausgeschlossen ... Primitive.dispatch KOSTET NICHTS").
;
; Save/restore makes the number SELF time: a primitive that re-enters the VM
; (`apply`, `sort` with a comparator, the sosofo/style primitives) is not
; charged for what the interpreter does underneath it. That is deliberate —
; the 1.72 G row it is meant to split is a leaf figure too.
;
; ★The BYTE column is the exact one and the reason to trust a ranking: the
; eval region's bump position before and after each dispatch, attributed with
; the same nesting discipline, so a primitive is charged its SELF allocation.
; The sampled column is kept beside it but is BIASED toward allocating code —
; the README's "Eichung" section has the proof and the magnitude.
;
; Measurement builds only (DZ_PRIM_PROF unset = the C side never arms the timer
; and never touches the depth stack; enter/exit stay a store, an increment and
; a store). Built by tests/dazzle/primprof/run.sh, never by build-cli.sh.

; The C shim (tests/dazzle/primprof/primprof.c). Scaly `int` is i64, which is
; C `long` on every LP64 target this tree serves — the widths are matched
; deliberately, cf. tests/abi/run.sh.
function pp_enter(id: int, host: pointer[void]) returns int extern
procedure pp_exit(prev: int, host: pointer[void]) extern
procedure pp_name_id(name: pointer[const_char], id: int) extern
procedure pp_start() extern

define PrimProf
{
    ; Publish `id` as the running primitive and take the eval region's bump
    ; position; the result must be handed back to `leave` at the end of the
    ; dispatch. `host` is read AGAIN at the exit rather than reused, because an
    ; eval-bracket switch inside the dispatch changes the region — the same
    ; discipline Escape.tick/tock keeps.
    procedure enter(id: int, mutable host: pointer[void]) returns int
        pp_enter(id, host)

    ; `exit` is not usable as a name here (it collides with the libc extern in
    ; scope at the call sites), hence `leave`.
    procedure leave(prev: int, mutable host: pointer[void])
        pp_exit(prev, host)

    ; Interpreter.install_primitive / install_x_primitive, so the report can
    ; print names rather than ids.
    procedure name_id(mutable name: pointer[const_char], id: int)
        pp_name_id(name, id)

    ; Interpreter.install_primitives, once, at engine setup.
    procedure start()
        pp_start()
}
